[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40291"] :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n26{x}_{1}=26\\cdot \\frac{7}{13}=14.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40401/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "183a08ec-af7c-57e0-b23e-2501443c5acc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40401/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "cbdc191a-0db6-5f8e-93ba-008409d008d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40401/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "107a1ac2-0019-5d7a-905a-5e8d42f29d55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40401/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "0486cbc8-7667-5613-a544-9495d38a8ca9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40401/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883