ed}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot (-4)+(-4)\\cdot 2}{{(-4)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20-8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}=5\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{5})=-7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-102337/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102337"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "b4ca6f8f-e7ab-57e1-b972-28b11b2674ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "027cff53-b458-5365-9f96-3449780f79a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "06300a6b-bd04-5016-8397-5cd808e28ad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "b3887c32-2361-5a41-8b20-24819bdce57f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "98dab1af-5e5d-565d-ace9-6340cc118d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98853296-ef75-5709-97c4-8dc7e236856c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81103/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer-field/choices ["q-81103/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" "q-81103/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" "q-81103/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-81103/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" "q-81103/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81103" :question/id #uuid "cea8b9f0-0696-5c6a-80c2-c39460b290e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-81103" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $15{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-3)}{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+12}{1+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n15{x}_{1}=15\\cdot \\frac{7}{5}=21.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87