er-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81142" :question/id #uuid "c22da228-1825-58b8-9f3c-add207e837ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-81142" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\sqrt{6}{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{6}}-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}{x}_{2}=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81142/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81142"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40293/selection/75890b30324487c8ca7d62d2c5a5e70e5a46b62a60147704a34309cbe4cf7b01" :answer/id #uuid "f183ec17-9e53-5099-90f6-6c9d8f4d941b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i