0e-555c-bafa-19ac086a5c9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-40293" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]}$  of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{25}{\\sqrt{26}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40293/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102322/selection/e5b0aaf9a55d5a12e77e3faeed1e31c2d2b441f93778222c04da8f53f9a2829e" :answer/id #uuid "59780a65-0686-5308-ae83-3a9c09a2682d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102322/selection/3030d2fd4812d8a96e7dd7370b709730aec4ad9edca4e56eab412965b009b2f0" :answer/id #uuid "b354047d-d921-5251-8048-7155b847509f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a